 The one finding, the missing perspective record, is answered. `docs/plans/WI-957/plan.perspectives.toml` covers SR-241, LLR-341 and TC-371, and `hats.py record ... --check --strict` reports no findings when I run it. PERFORMANCE produced SR-241, and each other applicable hat carries a stated no-finding I judge adequate. SECURITY: a read-only gate over a prior record adds no credential or irreversible authority. INTEGRITY-RECOVERABILITY: it writes nothing and refuses before any brief. TEST-ENGINEER and CONSISTENCY: one walk and one shared digest, every arm driven -> why it is ready: one decision (when a review brief may render), at a real boundary (the attended review route's output). Its acceptance is an observable condition with its pass lines, and its derivation is recorded, argued and reviewable. One observation, not a finding: its acceptance states no walk depth, while LLR-341 refuses past 64 commits. That bound fails closed, toward a refusal that names its recording step. It sits far outside what any supported workflow lays between an attest and a review, and it is the same design limit SR-156's governing walk carries unstated, so the SR's promise is not narrowed on any reachable path.\n- [APPROVE] LLR-341 -> the obligation: resolve the reviewed commit and search it, then its first-parent ancestors while their non-record identities stay equal, without peeling, for one verified review-bar record whose tests digest equals the round's, equivalent spellings and orderings giving one digest. Refuse, writing no brief, on an absent, malformed or unverified record, another bar (landing or no-bar included), another test set, a changed non-record path, or no verified record among the first 64 commits examined, the reviewed commit included. Name the commit, the cause, both compared values where the cause compares, and the attest step with the lane and the round's test list. On success, report the attested commit and digest. The search reads the record and never runs the bar -> what its chain shows: both of sitting 003's findings are answered. The bound is now a stated threshold (64 commits, counted from and including the reviewed commit), and TC-371 drives it both ways. The coordinator-cycle clause has left the row: that skill is this repository's own unshipped tooling, so its text pin stays a plain test outside the spine, and the never-approved TC-372 is retired on its record (`docs/log.d/retired/TC-372.md`). The row now states one decision, and every arm decomposes SR-241 -> why it is ready: the contract is refactor-proof (inputs, the stopping rule, each refusal and what it names, the success report). It names no code symbol (the attest step is the CLI verb, a boundary) and has no `shall`. Every arm has a TC-371 clause and a named case. It carries no own Hat-Refs, which is right: its parent's PERFORMANCE lens already says why it exists.\n- [APPROVE] TC-371 -> the obligation: on real lane commits, drive every refusal (no record, malformed, another tree or parent with both values asserted, another bar, another test set, a work commit above, the walk bound at 63 and 65 commits above the attested one) and the render paths (a matching record, record-only commits above it), and drive a record written by the attestation route rendered under a reordered equivalent test list -> what its chain shows: the third finding is answered. Expected now states the tree-or-parent both-values clause and the walk-bound clause, and the Method asserts both. The new case `test_a_search_past_the_walk_bound_refuses` exists and reads exactly so: 63 empty commits above the attested one render (the attested commit is the 64th examined), two more refuse, naming the bound, and its adequacy witness catches both an unbounded walk and an early refusal. Every arms-map row maps to a named, existing case. Verifies is SR-241, LLR-341, IF-288 and IF-289, each held by what the row drives -> why it is ready: Expected states the observable conditions and their pass lines, and nothing LLR-341 or SR-241 says goes unclaimed. Automated, Level and Tier are unambiguous, and Full is honest for real git fixtures with a 65-commit walk.\n\nOUTCOME: APPROVE rows=3\n\nSITTING: JUDGED kinds=first-approval\n"}}}
